# cahunEthics: hunter responsibilities and ethics in Ontario law and ministry guidance.
# Sources: FWCA ss. 5 to 8, 11, 21, 31, 36, 48, 50, 52; O. Reg. 665/98 ss. 34.1, 55;
# Hunting Regulations Summary 2026; ontario.ca Bear Wise page.
# Stems ask for a fact a trained candidate knows; every option is a lawful-sounding candidate.
SEG = "ETH"
CAT = "cahunEthics"
Q = [
('Section 36 bans abandoning game so that its flesh becomes unfit to eat. Which of these does that rule NOT cover?',
 'A coyote', ['A black bear', 'A white-tailed deer', 'A ruffed grouse'],
 'The meat rule covers game wildlife other than furbearing mammals, black bear included. For a furbearer such as a coyote, the hunter must not abandon or spoil the pelt instead.'),
('A hunter kills a raccoon. Under section 36, what must they not abandon or let spoil?',
 'The pelt', ['The meat', 'The skull', 'The tail'],
 'Section 36 (3) says a hunter or trapper who kills a furbearing mammal shall not abandon the pelt or let it be spoiled or destroyed.'),
('Without a trapping licence, the den of which animal may a person intentionally damage?',
 'A red fox', ['A raccoon', 'A mink', 'A river otter'],
 'Section 8 (2) bans intentionally damaging the den of a furbearing mammal, other than a fox or skunk, unless the person holds a licence to trap furbearers.'),
('During which months is it illegal to shoot a bear cub or a female bear with a cub?',
 'May and June', ['April and May', 'June and July', 'September and October'],
 'Section 55 bans shooting or trying to shoot a cub, or a female with a cub, during any part of a bear season that falls in May or June. A cub is a bear born that year.'),
('Under section 8 of the Act, who may damage a beaver dam without a trapping licence?',
 'An owner protecting their property', ['A licensed small game hunter', 'A deer hunter crossing a creek', 'Anyone during an open season'],
 'Section 8 (3) bans damaging or destroying a beaver dam unless the person holds a licence to trap furbearers, but section 8 (4) lets a person or their agent do it to protect their property.'),
('Who may sell the carcass of a furbearing mammal, pelt included, without any other licence?',
 'The trapper who trapped it', ['The hunter who shot it', 'A farmer who shot it', 'Any licensed hunter'],
 'Section 48 bans selling game wildlife except under a licence, but section 48 (3) lets the holder of a licence to trap furbearers sell all or part of a furbearer they trapped.'),
('Which part of a black bear is illegal to possess once it is removed from the carcass?',
 'The gall bladder', ['The cleaned skull', 'The claws', 'The tanned hide'],
 "Section 50 bans possessing a black bear gall bladder that has been removed from the bear's carcass."),
("Which of these does section 11 of the Act ban, except with the Minister's authorization?",
 'Paying a bounty for coyotes', ['Selling a trapped mink pelt', 'Hiring a bear hunting service', 'Buying a game farm pheasant'],
 'Section 11 bans paying or accepting a bounty and hunting or trapping for gain. Trappers may sell pelts, and bear hunting services and licensed game farms operate under their own licences.'),
('Under section 52, when may a restaurant list game wildlife on its menu without special authorization?',
 'When it was lawfully purchased', ['When a hunter donated it', 'When it was inspected', 'When it is served at cost'],
 'Section 52 bans listing game on a menu or charging for serving it, except game propagated under a licence or lawfully purchased, or with the Minister\'s authorization.'),
('Under section 31, which animal may a landowner never kill to protect their property, even with good reason?',
 'A moose', ['A raccoon', 'A striped skunk', 'A woodchuck'],
 'Section 31 lets a person kill wildlife damaging their property on their land, but never a moose or woodland caribou, and a deer or elk only with the Minister\'s authorization.'),
("A farmer wants a neighbour to kill raccoons raiding their corn. Under section 31, what does the neighbour need?",
 "The Minister's authorization", ['A small game licence', 'A trapping licence', "The farmer's written consent"],
 "Section 31 (2) lets a person use an agent only if the agent has the Minister's authorization or belongs to a class of agents prescribed by the regulations."),
('What must a hunter have before hunting double-crested cormorant?',
 'A way to retrieve the birds', ['A federal migratory permit', 'A cormorant tag', 'A licence to trap birds'],
 'Section 34.1 bans hunting double-crested cormorant without adequate means to retrieve any bird killed or injured, and a bird retrieved alive must be killed at once.'),
('Which of these birds may NOT be hunted in Ontario?',
 'A red-tailed hawk', ['A ruffed grouse', 'A wild turkey', 'A European starling'],
 'Section 5 bans hunting specially protected wildlife, which includes raptors such as hawks, and any wild bird that is not a game bird apart from a short list such as starlings and crows.'),
("The nest and eggs of which bird may be taken without the Minister's authorization?",
 'A house sparrow', ['A ruffed grouse', 'A wild turkey', 'A blue jay'],
 'Section 7 bans destroying, taking or possessing the nest or eggs of any bird wild by nature, except the American crow, brown-headed cowbird, common grackle, house sparrow, red-winged blackbird and starling.'),
('A black bear is killed in self-defence at a cottage. Under Bear Wise guidance, what must follow?',
 'Report it to the ministry', ['Invalidate a bear tag for it', 'Keep the hide and skull', 'Bury it where it fell'],
 'Bear Wise guidance says killing a bear in self-defence must be a last resort, done lawfully, safely and humanely. No licence is needed, but the kill must be reported to the ministry.'),
('For which bird may the meat spoilage rules of section 36 be set aside in prescribed circumstances?',
 'Double-crested cormorant', ['Canada goose', 'Ruffed grouse', 'Sharp-tailed grouse'],
 'Section 36 (2.1) says the rules against abandoning game and letting its flesh spoil do not apply to double-crested cormorant in the circumstances the regulations prescribe.'),
('Which of these may a licensed trapper hunt on their trapline without another licence?',
 'Black bear', ['White-tailed deer', 'Moose', 'Wild turkey'],
 'Section 6 (2) lets a trapper, in the area of the licence, hunt black bear and game mammals other than deer, moose, caribou and elk, and game birds other than wild turkey.'),
('Under section 11 (2), who may hunt for hire or gain without the Minister\'s authorization?',
 'A licensed guide', ['A hunt camp owner', 'A meat hunter for neighbours', 'A wildlife film crew'],
 'Section 11 bans hunting for hire or gain, but it does not apply to a guide or to a provider of black bear hunting services, nor to the person who hires them.'),
('Which of these may never be killed or captured with a trap or baited line?',
 'A ruffed grouse', ['A snowshoe hare', 'A gray squirrel', 'A cottontail'],
 'Section 21 (3) of the Act bans taking a game bird with a trap or baited line. A small game licence lets its holder take hares, cottontails and squirrels in a box trap, cage trap or net.'),
('A hunter wants to sell venison from a deer they lawfully shot. What does section 48 of the Act say?',
 'Not without a licence', ['Allowed once inspected', 'Allowed at cost only', 'Allowed to neighbours'],
 'Section 48 bans buying or selling game wildlife, including its parts, except under a licence and the regulations. Wild game meat is not government inspected.'),
]
